body: "GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/437#issuecomment-5575662594\n\nReproduced a remaining regression in **pm-cli 2026.9.7** on Linux / Node 22.20.0, with `--no-extensions` on every command. Reusing this closed canonical issue after searching all issue states for `claim receipt`, `claim output`, and `claim compact` and reviewing #195 and #437.\n\nIn a fresh temporary working directory:\n\n```bash\nexport PM_AUTHOR=claim-output-repro\npm init probe --json --no-extensions\npm create Task 'Mutation output reproduction' --id probe-claim \\\n  --description 'Reproduce claim output without custom extensions' \\\n  --status open --priority 2 --create-mode progressive --json --no-extensions\npm claim probe-claim --json --no-extensions\n```\n\n`create` emits the documented flat `{id, status, changed_field_count}` receipt (75 bytes in this reproduction). `claim` instead emits `{item, claimed_by, previous_assignee, forced}` with the full item (550 bytes even for this tiny fixture), no top-level `id` or `status`, and no `changed_field_count`. Claiming a populated real project epic repeats its description and complete comments, making the discrepancy substantially larger.\n\nThe current root `--help` says mutations emit a flat receipt, so callers following that documented contract cannot parse `claim` like `create`/`update`. Output projection is not a workaround: `claim --output-include item.id,item.status` correctly rejects read-only output controls.\n\nPlease include `claim` in the default compact mutation contract, retaining claim-specific outcome/ownership fields where necessary and an explicit full-output opt-in. This is reproducible without project custom extensions; no extension issue is implicated.\n\n\nCurrent-checkout verification: isolated no-extension CLI create emits 71 bytes with id/status/changed_field_count; claim emits 517 bytes with item/claimed_by/previous_assignee/forced and no top-level id/status/change count. Synthetic fixture only."
